I am still standing at Jonas's desk.
I take my phone out of my pocket.
I look for the route for Friday evening.
I see that Nele does not live in the center.
Her flat is a bit further out.
"I will travel directly from the office," I say to Jonas.
"I will take the U-Bahn."
Jonas looks at my phone.
He shows me a good route on the screen.
"This connection is very fast," he says.
"I think that you only have to change trains once."
I read the travel times exactly.
The journey will take almost forty minutes.
"That fits perfectly," I answer.
"I thank you for the help, Jonas."
"You are welcome!" he answers.
Now the route is planned.
